# Third-party materials and sources

## Code library

**astronomy-engine (v2.1.19)** — Sun, Moon, Earth positions and DSN
elevations (inlined in `index.html`).
Author: Don Cross, https://github.com/cosinekitty/astronomy
Terms: MIT. Its copyright notice is kept in the inlined library header.

## Published formulas (no data copied)

- **Meeus, *Astronomical Algorithms*, ch. 53** — libration formulas in
  `physics.js`. Author: Jean Meeus. Formulas only; no text or tables copied,
  cited.
- **Solar constant 1360.8 W/m²** — used on the Power tab. Source: Kopp, G.
  and Lean, J. L. (2011), *Geophysical Research Letters* 38, L01706,
  doi:10.1029/2010GL045777 (SORCE/TIM, LASP). One published value, cited; no
  data copied.

## NASA terrain and elevation data

- **LOLA 5 m south-pole DEM** (Site01 `surf` + `toterr`) — terrain and
  ground-error maps. Source: NASA LRO/LOLA, PGDA (Mazarico, Barker et al.).
  NASA data, cited as NASA/GSFC/LOLA.
- **AVGVISIB_85S_060M_201608** (+ `.LBL`) — used in Check 1. Source: NASA
  LOLA team, PGDA. NASA data, cited.
- **LDEM_60S_60MPP_ADJ** (cropped to 200 km, `far_LDEM_60S_60MPP_ADJ.tif`)
  and **LDEM_83S_10MPP_ADJ** (cropped, cross-check only) — far terrain beyond
  the 5 m ground. Source: NASA LRO/LOLA, PGDA,
  https://pgda.gsfc.nasa.gov/products/90. NASA data, cited as NASA/GSFC/LOLA.
- **Site04 5 m DEM and error map; Site01 error map; NASA's 100 alternative
  grounds (clones) for Site01 and Site04** — second site, trust label, Check
  2. Source: NASA LRO/LOLA, PGDA, https://pgda.gsfc.nasa.gov/products/78.
  NASA data, cited.

## NASA imagery

- **Moon colour map** (`moon_4096.jpg`, downsized from the 8k "CGI Moon
  Kit") — Moon globe. Source: NASA Scientific Visualization Studio,
  https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4720; visualization by Ernie Wright (USRA), LRO
  camera + LOLA data. NASA media; credit "NASA/GSFC/Scientific Visualization
  Studio".
- **Earth picture** (`earth_bm4096.jpg`, replaces the old `earth.jpg`) —
  Earth in 3D view. Source: NASA Blue Marble: Next Generation with
  Topography and Bathymetry (January 2004), NASA Earth Observatory (Reto
  Stöckli),
  https://science.nasa.gov/earth/earth-observatory/blue-marble-next-generation/base-topography-bathymetry/.
  Downloaded by the team (original 5400 x 2700, 2.5 MB, sent as a zip),
  reduced to 4096 x 2048. NASA imagery; credit "NASA Earth Observatory".
  Check NASA Earth Observatory's image-use page for the exact credit wording
  before submitting.
- **LROC NAC south-pole controlled mosaic**
  `NAC_POLE_SOUTH_CM_005_P892S2250` (cropped for Site 01 and Site 04) — Check
  3 on the page. Source: NASA LROC / Arizona State University, PDS. NASA
  data, cited.
- **LROC NAC south-pole controlled mosaics**
  `NAC_POLE_SOUTH_CM_125_P892S2250` and `NAC_POLE_SOUTH_CM_335_P892S2250`
  (cropped for Site 01 and Site 04) — further photo checks in the notes
  (`exp7`), not shown on the page. Source: NASA LROC / Arizona State
  University, PDS. NASA data, cited.

## NASA mission data

**JPL DSN Telecommunications Link Design Handbook, 810-005, Module 301
(Rev. O, 1 July 2024)**, Table 5 and the 6 degree minimum elevation — Comms
tab: station positions of DSS-14, DSS-43, DSS-63 (WGS 84) and minimum
elevation. Source: NASA JPL / Caltech, https://deepspace.jpl.nasa.gov/dsndocs/810-005/.

Page wording: "Source: NASA JPL, DSN Telecommunications Link Design
Handbook 810-005, Module 301. Only published numbers are used. No
endorsement is implied." Published numbers only; no text or figures copied.
The handbook's own reuse terms were not read (host unreachable from the
workspace); check before submitting.

